@startuml
title 03  |  Conversational recommendation run

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #37678C
  LifeLineBorderColor #A9BAC8
  ParticipantBorderColor #476782
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF3FA
  ActorBorderColor #476782
  ActorBackgroundColor #EAF3FA
  GroupBorderColor #91AAC0
  GroupBackgroundColor #F5F9FC
  NoteBorderColor #D7B766
  NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E7
}

actor Shopper
boundary "Streamlit UI" as UI
control "Run controller" as Controller
control "Trusted controller\n(fixed five-role graph)" as Graph
control "Shared services" as Services
database "SQLite repository" as Store
control "Bounded model adapter" as Model

Shopper -> UI: Submit chat request
UI -> Controller: Create request version and run context
Controller -> Graph: Start bounded conversational run
Graph -> Model: Intake and Clarification\n(local chat only; no tools)
Model --> Graph: Candidate requirements or ambiguity

opt Missing required detail or ambiguous exclusion
  Graph --> Controller: Clarification request
  Controller --> UI: Ask for required detail
  UI --> Shopper: Show question
  Shopper -> UI: Supply correction
  UI -> Controller: Create new request version
  Controller -> Graph: Resume with validated requirements
end

Graph -> Services: Catalog Evidence role:\nsearch products and fetch details
Services -> Store: Read versioned evidence
Store --> Services: Facts and provenance
Services --> Graph: Candidates and limitations
Graph -> Graph: Validate typed evidence handoff
Graph -> Services: Review Evidence role:\nanalyze permitted reviews
Services --> Graph: Validated review artifact or unavailable
Graph -> Services: Policy and Ranking role:\nscreen ingredients; hard-filter, then rank
Services --> Graph: Eligible IDs, fixed scores, reasons

alt Eligible products
  Graph -> Model: Explanation and Citation role:\nselected evidence only
  Model --> Graph: Candidate claims or failure
  Graph -> Services: Validate citation identity and support
  Services --> Graph: Supported text or factual fallback
  Graph --> Controller: Validated comparison
else No eligible products
  Graph --> Controller: Empty result and actual limiting reasons
end

Controller -> Controller: Accept only current request version
Controller --> UI: Publish validated current state
UI --> Shopper: Show result, limits, and progress

note over Controller, Services
  Roles return only to the controller. They cannot
  delegate, select tools, persist, or bypass validation.
  The structured form calls these services directly;
  eligibility and numeric scores must match chat.
end note
@enduml
